<article class="env-lemma" id="0DPE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DPE">Lemma <span data-tag="0DPE">108.7.4</span>.</a> Let $B$ be an algebraic space. Let $\pi : X \to Y$ be an open immersion of algebraic spaces which are separated and of finite presentation over $B$. Then $\pi $ induces an open immersion $\mathrm{Hilb}_{X/B} \to \mathrm{Hilb}_{Y/B}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: If $Z \subset X_ T$ is a closed subscheme which is proper over $T$, then $Z$ is also closed in $Y_ T$. Thus we obtain the transformation $\mathrm{Hilb}_{X/B} \to \mathrm{Hilb}_{Y/B}$. If $Z \subset Y_ T$ is an element of $\mathrm{Hilb}_{Y/B}(T)$ and for $t \in T$ we have $|Z_ t| \subset |X_ t|$, then the same is true for $t' \in T$ in a neighbourhood of $t$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>